it's getting closer we are now less than  a month  from election day anyone planning to  cast a ballot in nevada needs to be  registered to vote of course there are  certain deadlines to do that  including one that ends tomorrow a news  now reporter kristen drummond shows us  what voters need to know  mark your calendars for voter  registration dates each  voter registration method has a  different deadline  wayne thorley is deputy secretary of  state for elections  he says the first major deadline is  tuesday october 6.  that's the last day anyone can submit a  paper voter registration application  the form can be found online the dmv  county election  office or state agencies providing  public assistance  the paper allows anyone without a state  license or id  to register and vote in nevada you can  use the last four of your social  security number  for the identification field if you miss  the deadline  don't worry there are two other ways to  register going forward  on the secretary of state website or a  polling place  but state law requires a state license  or  id dmv has set up a  on saturdays in the morning appointments  for new residents only to obtain a  driver's license or id card  same day registration and early voting  starts october 17th  and finishes october 30th online  registration ends at midnight of october  29th  anyone with a nevada license or id can  also register november 3rd  election day but register soon to ensure  you receive a mail ballot  this year anybody who registers to vote  on  or before october 15th  will get a ballot sent to them in the  mail anybody that registers to vote  after october 15 must vote in person  different ways to guarantee you can cast  a ballot kristen drummond 8 news now  mail ballots are being sent to all  registered voters because of the  pandemic no one needs to request an  absentee ballot this year  clark county will start mailing the  ballots on october 10th
 

